1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:02,840
Welcome to Canva.

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:10,360
What I want to show you is how this very powerful online tool, Canva.com, can be used to support the

3
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:16,840
teaching approach of the activated classroom, which is specifically the pedagogy of chaos.

4
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:20,360
Now, you might think chaos is a bad thing, but chaos is something that we have to deal with all the

5
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:20,920
time.

6
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:25,920
And when we've got too much information or too little information or even conflicting information,

7
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:31,080
what is important is being able to take all of that information together and put it into something that

8
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:34,160
brings it succinctly down to a visual representation.

9
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:39,120
And one of the ways that that is very powerfully done is through what are called infographics.

10
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:44,800
An infographic is essentially a whole lot of complex information that has been condensed into a visual

11
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:45,440
representation.

12
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:48,320
And that's what this pedagogy of chaos is about.

13
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:53,120
Trying to summarize, really distill the essence of our learning.

14
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,240
And Canva is a great site for doing that.

15
00:00:55,240 --> 00:01:01,040
So if you come across to Canva and choose infographic, you'll be presented with a whole range of templates.

16
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:06,280
All you now need to do is choose one that you think fits what you want to put together your summary.

17
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:10,200
So maybe you want to make a series of points so you could choose one like this.

18
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:15,680
Or you keep going down you'll see this the bulleted one, not as interesting in terms of not being as

19
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,000
graphical, but maybe there are ten things that you want to remember.

20
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:21,760
What a great way to succinctly bring them all together.

21
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,360
You can get quite visual.

22
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:24,480
Maybe you want to do it like this.

23
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:28,760
It shows four items that are key to you and so on and on it goes.

24
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:33,760
You'll notice that most of them have got free, meaning there's no cost, which is a big plus.

25
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:37,120
Some of them you do pay for, so just look out for that.

26
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:37,800
So it's interesting.

27
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:44,400
All you need to do is choose one which you think, well this would be a great one to to represent my

28
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,120
thinking.

29
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:53,160
So go down, pick an infographic that you think, well, I'm going to use this one as a visual image

30
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:56,960
of what I have learned on this particular course.

31
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:01,400
So I'd say, well, you know, the things I've learned, there's lots of them.

32
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:05,360
And I wonder what would be a great way for me to represent this.

33
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:10,360
And again, just by thinking about this for a few minutes, you are having to try and distill your learning

34
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:12,440
down to something that makes sense.

35
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:16,880
So let us pick one of these infographics to represent our learning.

36
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,240
Well, this one here looks fun.

37
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,480
We're going to pick it.

38
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,480
Let's play on.

39
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,880
So it's a free infographic.

40
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:27,560
Quite simply all you need to do is you can zoom in a little bit so you can see it more clearly.

41
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:30,440
And now you can edit it as simple as that.

42
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,880
You can click on any element and edit your learning.

43
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:44,200
If you want to change the font or the font size, simply click on it, go to the top and you can change

44
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:44,800
the font.

45
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,520
You can change colors, you can change all sorts of things.

46
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:52,800
It really is quite simple and it's now just a matter of putting your content down.

47
00:02:55,880 --> 00:03:01,160
If you want to insert something, an image again, this is also really, really simple.

48
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:05,560
There are a whole range of elements that can be inserted on the left hand side.

49
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:09,840
You will see an option to choose what elements you would like to insert.

50
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,400
And so you can search on these.

51
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:16,680
They can be icons, lines, illustrations, or you could just search over here for whatever the image

52
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:17,600
you are looking for.

53
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:21,640
So maybe you are looking for, um, HTML.

54
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,840
Immediately it's going to come up with a whole lot of images.

55
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:27,680
Again, if they are free, you can use them.

56
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:28,960
Some you are going to have to pay for.

57
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,480
So maybe I want to use this one here.

58
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:31,080
So I'll say yes.

59
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,440
That's exactly the one I want.

60
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:33,040
Click it.

61
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,520
It places it on the page.

62
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:39,360
You can now resize it and put it wherever you want to get rid of an image.

63
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,480
I don't want that one.

64
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:44,680
Click it, hit delete and I can put my image here.

65
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,840
Resizing is a simple process.

66
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:52,440
You can also upload your own images should you want to.

67
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:58,680
So if you did search for something and you weren't happy with oh, I don't like any of those, you can

68
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,280
go and upload your own image.

69
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,440
But I'm happy with this.

70
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,080
It's free.

71
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,160
It's to do with CSS.

72
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,120
That seems good enough.

73
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,440
Or I could take one of these.

74
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:10,280
Let's just take this one over here and I will use that.

75
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:25,800
Right.

76
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,440
So that is essentially the process.

77
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:28,800
You can continue doing that.

78
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:34,280
You simply edit each of the items and at the end of it you can produce for yourself a lovely visual

79
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:37,400
representation of the key things that you learned.

80
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:52,200
Once you're done, you can quite simply hit download and you can download your image.

81
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:56,400
You can download it as a PNG, JPEG, or a PDF as simple as that.

82
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:02,560
And at the end of the day, what you've now created is you've created a lovely, simple infographic

83
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,600
of what you've learned.

84
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:06,560
It's a great way to distill your learning and to remember it into the day.

85
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:09,640
You now have an image that summarizes the key points of what you've learned.

86
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,160
So over to you.

87
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,880
Take whatever it is you're learning about.

88
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:19,640
Get across to Canva and create for yourself a infographic representation of your learning, and you

89
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:24,880
will have just experienced the power of the activated classroom teaching, pedagogy of chaos and how

90
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:26,960
it will help you remember your learning.

